          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പ്രസ്താവന — prastāvana — \"a statement\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പോലീസ് അപകടത്തെക്കുറിച്ച് ഒരു പ്രസ്താവന ഇറക്കി. pōlīsŭ apakaṭattekkuṟiccŭ oru prastāvana iṟakki. The police issued a statement about the accident."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The formal word for what someone sets out in public, usually in writing."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പ്രസ്താവന (prastāvana) is borrowed from Sanskrit prastāvanā, \"a sounding forth; an introduction, a preface\" (Monier-Williams). In Malayalam it came to mean what someone sets forth in public."
            }
          ]
        },
