          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "സത്യാവസ്ഥ — satyāvastha — \"the real facts; the actual truth\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ലേഖകൻ സംഭവത്തിന്റെ സത്യാവസ്ഥ കണ്ടെത്തി. lēkhakan sambhavattinṟe satyāvastha kaṇṭetti. The correspondent found out the real facts of the incident."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Literally the state of the truth: സത്യം, truth, + അവസ്ഥ, a state."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "സത്യാവസ്ഥ (satyāvastha) is built from two Sanskrit words: satya, \"true; the truth\" (CDIAL 13112), and avasthā, \"a state, a condition\" (CDIAL 872). It names how things really stand, as against what people say."
            }
          ]
        },
